Classes
    .blueprint for creating objects 
        .is like a patient chart template: 
            .every patient has name, age, vitals; but each patient has different values
        .class defines structure, object is the actual patient


        class Patient:   - blueprint
            def __init__(self, name, age):   - constructor method to initialize object
                self.name = name      - self refers to the instance being created ( the object itself)
                self.age = age 

    .attributes are assigned inside the object (name, age) - these are the properties of the Patient
        .it is attaching data to the object 

.methods are always defined inside the class 
.self is a method parameter that refers to the instance of the class
__init__ is the constructor method that is automatically called when a new object is created from the class
.def is used to define a method inside a class 
.an instance is an individual object created from a class 
.an attribute is a variable that belongs to an instance of a class 
.object is a specific instance of a class that contains data(attributes) and methods(behaviors)
    .if the class is the blueprint, the object is the actual house built from that blueprint


    class - blueprint for creating objects
    .object - actual thing
    .instance - specific object created from a class
    .attribute - variable that belongs to an instance of a class
    .method - function defined inside a class  
            .describes the behaviors of the objects created from the class
    .self - refers to the instance of the class, used to access attributes and methods within the class


